18 0 obj
<< /A 67 0 R /Alt (Techniques for control of blast disease in rice. A graphical overview of rice blast control strategies is categorized into four groups: \(i\) Conventional techniques including pedigree breeding, mutation breeding, and backcross breeding; \(ii\) Molecular techniques such as QTL mapping, omics approaches, speed breeding, genomic selection, marker-assisted backcross breeding \(MABB\), marker-assisted selection \(MAS\), genomic selection, and genome-wide association studies \(GWAS\); \(iii\) Transgenic techniques comprising RNA interference, ectopic expression, and genome editing; and \(iv\) Future techniques highlighting nanotechnology, synthetic biology, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. The central image shows rice leaves with characteristic blast lesions.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 68 0 R /Alt <> /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
